    InLine(ty: Struct((size: Unsized, crate_idx: 0, docs: [
        "A phase angle in the angle unit `A`: the argument of a phasor, an NCO\'s phase, a motor\'s electrical angle. Same",
        "dimension, scale and symbol as `A`, but of the kind `phase angle` ([Kind::Named]), so it isn\'t a mechanical",
        "angle: `Phase<Turn>` converts to `Phase<Degree>`, not to [Turn]. The steps between them are named: `as_phase` and",
        "`as_plane_angle` (the same number), and `electrical(pole_pairs)` from a motor\'s mechanical angle to its electrical",
        "angle, the phase a field-oriented control\'s Park transform takes.",
        "",
        "```",
        "# #[cfg(feature = \"angle\")] {",
        "use exact_units::{Bam16, Fixed, PhaseBam16, prefix::One, units::{Degree, Phase, Turn}};",
        "",
        "let half = Fixed::<Phase<Turn>, One, f32>::new(0.5);",
        "assert_eq!(half.convert::<Phase<Degree>, One, f32>(), Some(Fixed::new(180.0)));",
        "// a rotor at 0.3 turn with 7 pole pairs is at 2.1 turns electrical, 0.1 turn of phase",
        "let mechanical: Bam16 = exact_units::fixed!(0.3);",
        "let phase: PhaseBam16 = mechanical.electrical(7);",
        "assert_eq!(phase.get(), 19661u16.wrapping_mul(7));",
        "# }",
        "```",
        "",
        "On the wire and in a unit\'s [UnitExpr] it is `A`: the kind is in the type, as for [Ohm].",
    ], ident: "Phase", generics: [
        (ident: "A", kind: Type),
    ], fields: Named([]), sparse: false, path: Some([
        "units",
    ]), instance_of: None, extra: Some((transparent: false, marker: Some(Phase))))), crate_idx: 0),
    InLine(ty: Struct((size: UnsizedFinalStructure, crate_idx: 0, docs: [
        "A value in unit `U` and prefix `P`, stored as `T`, within the bounds `B`: on the wire exactly `T`, the unit,",
        "prefix and bounds are only in the type. `shared_us: u64` becomes `shared: Fixed<Second, Micro, u64>` (or",
        "[Micros]`<u64>`) with the same bytes, and introspection shows `µs`.",
        "",
        "Where a `ww_si::Quantity` lets the device pick prefix and number type per value (and sends both), a `Fixed` has them fixed",
        "by the API: no prefix on the wire, no `NumericValue` on the device, so a `u64` here doesn\'t turn on `ww_numeric`\'s",
        "`u64` for the whole firmware.",
        "",
        "```",
        "use exact_units::{Fixed, Micros, prefix::{Micro, Milli}, units::Second};",
        "",
        "let t: Micros<u32> = Fixed::new(1500);",
        "assert_eq!(format!(\"{t}\"), \"1500 µs\");",
        "assert_eq!(format!(\"{t:#}\"), \"0.0015 s\");",
        "// exact conversions only: 1500 µs is not a whole number of ms",
        "assert_eq!(t.to::<Milli, u16>(), None);",
        "assert_eq!((t * 2).to::<Milli, u16>(), Some(Fixed::new(3)));",
        "assert_eq!(core::time::Duration::from(t), core::time::Duration::from_micros(1500));",
        "```",
        "",
        "`B` is [Unbounded] unless given, and stays out of the way then: `Fixed::new` and the operators exist for the",
        "three-parameter form. A bounded value is made with [try_new](Self::try_new) or [bounded](Self::bounded) and checked",
        "on every read from the wire:",
        "",
        "```",
        "use exact_units::{Fixed, Range, prefix::Milli, units::Second};",
        "",
        "type Timeout = Fixed<Second, Milli, u16, Range<1, 5000>>;",
        "assert!(Timeout::try_new(10).is_ok());",
        "assert!(Timeout::try_new(0).is_err());",
        "const LONG: Timeout = Timeout::bounded(5000);",
        "assert_eq!(LONG.get(), 5000);",
        "```",
        "",
        "A bound that doesn\'t fit the storage doesn\'t build:",
        "",
        "```compile_fail",
        "use exact_units::{Fixed, Range, prefix::One, units::Ratio};",
        "",
        "let _ = Fixed::<Ratio, One, u8, Range<-5, 300>>::try_new(5);",
        "```",
    ], ident: "Fixed", generics: [
        (ident: "U", kind: Type),
        (ident: "P", kind: Type),
        (ident: "T", kind: Type),
        (ident: "B", kind: Type),
    ], fields: Named([
        (ident: Some("value"), default: None, since: None, ty: Param(2), docs: [
            "The number of steps of `P`.",
        ], slot: None, series_opaque: false),
    ]), sparse: false, path: None, instance_of: None, extra: Some((transparent: true, marker: None)))), crate_idx: 0),
